# VII. Conclusion

** Whether the study is worth studying: it is worth studying.

The logic of e-investment is relatively clear: the core is "buying a high-quality game cash flow machine at a reasonably low price." Unlike Alibaba (which needs to judge the return on AI investment) and more than a thousand pieces (which need to judge Temu's future), the core variables of e-finance are simpler – whether the long-term IP can continue to maintain + the new game line or not.

Currently, about 16 times the PE, 12 times the net cash net EVI/net profit, is an objective margin for a company with ROE stable at 22-24% and a Māori rate of 70%. It is also important to recognize that the grid-friendly growth ceiling is limited, and business is highly concentrated in a single area of games, and that 16 times the PE may already partly reflect these structural features.

